      "message": "fix(2d): keep contour leads on the air side at a closed ring's seam\n\nThe seam of a round-cornered outside ring falls on a fitted corner arc.\nThe arc's end tangent is a hair off the ring's first chord, toward the\nmaterial. A linear lead-out along it went back across the ring's second\nmove, and verify held the post with one crossing on each level. The\nlead-in had the same fault on a conventional cut.\n\nOn a closed ring that bends to the air side at the seam, the lead-out\ntangent is now mirrored across the start tangent, and the lead-in\ntangent across the end tangent. Other seams and open walks keep their\ntangents.\n\nFixes #3019\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
